  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 204 PM CDT Thu Aug 6 2026\n\nA cold front is forecast to move in across the southwest\nbringing some windy conditions out west this afternoon. In \naddition relative humidity is forecast to be around be around 10\nto 20 percent out west with windy conditions this afternoon will\nlead to Red Flag conditions across the portions of western \nNorth Dakota. Read the fire weather discussion for more \ninformation. Temperatures this afternoon are forecast to warm \ninto the 90s across the state. The cold front will bring \nslightly cooler temperatures to the region tomorrow with highs \nforecast to be in the 70-80s. Another front will move through \nthe region Friday afternoon bringing a wind shift.\n\nNorthwesterly flow will continue into weekend, however we will\nbe on the equatorward side of the upper level flow. This will \nhinder any expected precipitation chances. Thus, dry conditions \nwill continue through the weekend. Winds will remain light \nkeeping critical fire weather conditions at bay. Although Sunday\ncould be a bit breezy across the south central. Temperatures \nwill remain in the in the 80s this weekend with the southwest \ntouching the 90s by Sunday. The pattern may be a bit more active\nby the middle of next week as the flow shifts from \nNorthwesterly to quasi zonal which could bring forth some low to\nmedium chances for showers and thunderstorms. This will also \ncause the temperatures to drop down into the 70s and 80s.",
